# The tree's delete confirm opens with Cancel focused — as the reference
# editor focuses it: a destructive box's Enter must not be the
# destructive act (`src/app/trash.zig`). That half is by design and this
# file does not contest it.
#
# The SILENT half had no rationale anywhere. Enter on `Delete a.txt?`
# tore the dialog down with no toast and no statusline line, which on
# screen is indistinguishable from a delete that worked — and Enter is
# the likeliest key on any dialog. The cancel now says so, and names the
# key that does delete.
write a.txt "aa"
command view.focus_tree
key r
key end
command file.delete
expect screen contains "Delete a.txt?"
key enter
wait 400
# The by-design half: the file survives.
expect file a.txt contains "aa"
# The open half: the app says the delete did not happen, and how to.
expect screen contains "cancelled"
expect screen contains "a.txt kept"
expect screen contains "`d` deletes"
